  "as_of": "2014-03-27",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would ban exports of live livestock intended for slaughter overseas by inserting a new prohibition mechanism into Australia's existing export control legislation.",
   "It would cover cattle, calves, sheep, lambs, goats and other prescribed animals where they were intended to be exported and slaughtered outside Australia.",
   "The substantive provisions would commence on the day after Royal Assent, with the export ban operating through deemed regulations under the Export Control Act."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "A statutory definition would identify the livestock intended for overseas slaughter covered by the new section.",
   "Regulations would be treated as declaring that livestock to be prescribed goods.",
   "Regulations would also be treated as imposing an absolute prohibition on exporting that livestock."
  ],
  "affected": "Exporters of live livestock for slaughter overseas would be affected.",
